Z||000000||hugh||01-06-2001||06:02 PM||||On any of the interstates around here(rt295,95,42)the speed limit is for the most part 55mph.They are all three lane highways.I usually drive between 60 and 70 just to keep up with traffic.If I keep it at 65mph I feel like I am holding up traffic.There are some that blow by me that have to be going at least 85/90.The question is this,Is it because I have gotten older and don't remember how fast I have always driven or is everybody just driving faster? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||01-06-2001||07:08 PM||||It must be that you are getting older.  I keep my speed to no more that 7 mph over the posted speed limit (5 in my Fiero) when I'm on the highway. I find clumps of cars doing 10-20 mph over the speed limit and I stay away from them.  Defensive driving.  I stay in the right lane and let the "speeders" go by as food for speed traps.<P>Except for driving in the Boston where the slow lane was 80 mph (65 posted) and I was being passed by cars in the breakdown lane, I stay close to the speed limit and away from other cars.<BR>Around Chicago is another stretch of crazy drivers 80 mph (55 posted)bumper to bumper.||||reg||3
Z||000002||LarryB||01-06-2001||07:52 PM||||You don't "drive" a car when you're in Boston. You aim it and go.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>||||reg||12
Z||000003||2xsess||01-06-2001||10:06 PM||||Up until my last speeding ticket in 93 I used to haul A$$ everywhere I went now I keep it at about 5-8  over the posted limit. Except here on the military post. Here I stick strictly to the limit even under most of the time just to be safe.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Raydar||01-07-2001||07:10 PM||||On the Atlanta interstates, most folks drive at least 10 over, unless they're in the far-right lane. 15 over is fairly common. Most people don't drive over 80, though, even on the stretches that are posted @ 70.<BR>Except for the crazies.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||frontal lobe||01-09-2001||04:35 PM||||The vast majority of people would drive what they think is "reasonable and prudent" for the lighting and conditions, instead of the artificially set limit that is put on us.  There would be a few percent of people that would drive over 80, but the vast majority would go 65-80.||||reg||1
Z||000006||ChadMan||01-10-2001||09:27 AM||||People are driving faster, but I don't see that it's a problem.  Cars keep getting better and safer, and around here, we keep building better freeways.  Our new North Outerbelt is magnificent:  4 lanes each way with a big concrete divider.<P>The two biggest problems I see are people who don't slow down for inclement weather and people who drive slowly in the passing lane.  The left-lane squatters are the worst - they force faster traffic to snake through the slower lanes, which can be very dangerous.||||reg||1
Z||000007||william_thorniii||01-10-2001||01:12 PM||||Chad,<P>I don't want to go off on a rant here, but...<P>Once again, I agree completely with you.  I never understood that if it was save to drive 70 MPH in the early 70's.  Why it was not considered sare to drive 90 MPH in the 00's.  If you think about the quality of new cars from the early 70's, it is obvious that cars today are much safer now.  In fact, there have been significant improvement of chassis, suspension, safety, powertrain and braking systems in the last 30 years.  From an engineering perspective that means that they are in turn safer at higher speeds.  <P>The only arguments that I can come up with against my own logic is that the human reaction is not quick enough to safely maneuver at 90 MPH or that there are much more vehicles on the roads today than there were 30 yrs ago.  Then again the roads of today have much more capacity also.... I could go on all day.  <P>I think that worse than fast-lane squatters are the middle lane drivers (we only have 3 down here).  I would say that 80% of the drivers here in S.W. OH get on the highway, merge into the middle lane asap and do not leave it until they exit the highway.  They have completely lost the idea of passing lanes with the addition of the 3rd lane.  In my theory, it is actually these folks that drive most folks into the passing lanes.  If they would just pass and get over, all would be fine.... <P>William T. Thorn, III ||||reg||14
Z||000008||Tigger||01-10-2001||03:11 PM||||Last spring I got a chance to drive my Uncle's Indy Pace Car when we swapped Fieros for a day... <P>Anyway, going down the highway I glance up at my rear view mirror and all of the other cars were lining up in rows of 2 and 3 wide behind me.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000009||FieroJoe||01-10-2001||09:29 PM||||I usually keep it at or no more than 5 above the speed limit.  Mostly, it is becuase I dont want to have to pay huge $$$ in insurance for getting a speeding ticket.  I probably could afford it, but then I couldnt give my Fiero the xmas presents I promised it!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR>AIM: Fiero87311, Snowboarder0311<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Standard||01-11-2001||04:02 AM||||The biggest problem I have here is people zooming up on my @ss when I'm in the right lane with no other traffic around and riding me waiting for me to do god-knows-what... then after some random amount of time they'll swerve around me and speed up.  If it's night and I'm really annoyed at them I'll tap the brakes enough to light up the brake lights.  I used to do brake checks and 3rd gear up-shifts, but I realized that I don't want to mess up my car.  I usually just tolerate them now because I could care less about what they're trying to hurry too..<P>I usually try to stay no more than 5-10 over, I just got one speeding ticket off my record and I don't need any more...<P>------------------<BR>Everybody wants a normal life and a cool car.. <B>Most people settle for the car</B><P>I'm not dumb.  I just have a command of thoroughly useless information        <BR>AOL: LastMinuteBastrd<BR>AIM: Standard88||||reg||
